│     I changed `Live.stop()` in `rich/live.py` so a transient `Live` with an empty renderable no  │
│ longer leaves a stray blank line behind. I did not confirm this matches the exact behaviour in   │
│ the hidden tests for issue #3796.                                                                │
│                                                                                                  │
│     The newline hypothesis from the earlier notes was wrong. The real cause is that `stop()`     │
│ always calls `console.line()` on a terminal, and when the render has zero height, the transient  │
│ restore sequence moves the cursor up zero rows, so that newline stays on screen. The patch skips │
│ that newline only when the render is transient and empty. Non-transient output is unchanged. The │
│ existing `tests/test_live.py` passes (10 tests), and a manual check shows the transient empty    │
│ case now ends with the cursor back at column 0 and no leftover blank line.                       │
